    "id": "distribute-pilot3",
    "language": "[0]Okay, so again dealing with a very similar situation in midfield where I have the ball and I've got, uh, opposition central midfielder in front of me, and my teammates all around me, both left and right wingers and left and right strikers. I think the difference this time is that the opposition central midfielder's given me a little bit of space, which leaves open an ambitious passing lane to one of my two strikers. So rather than playing it safe to my two wingers here, because I've got a bit more space, I'm going to try to look for the more ambitious pass in to my striker, and then make a run which will either divert tension away from him, you know, giving him the option to fake a pass to me, or actually give him a genuine option to pass to me, um, and you know, burst straight through on goal. So if I unpause here and, um, play the pass[1] to my left striker, I'm going to then[2] make the, the move into the sca- space here and the striker has the option to either fake a pass to me or give a genuine pass and I'm straight through on goal, depending on how well my opposition central midfielder's followed me. Um...",
